As you might have guessed from the subject line, this contains some spoilers.

After I made my first ascensions of nethack for the first few times,
it appeared to me that the upper limit of scores one can get in this
game is around 2-6 million points. This is due to the fact that the
only ways one can get points in this game are:

1) Killing monsters: You can get up to 2000 points for killing some of the
   meaner monsters, but trying to up your score by several million at this
   rate (by reverse genociding trolls for instance) is slow and boring.
2) Getting gold: Unfortunately, this is limited by the amount of gold that
   you can find in the dungeon, as well as by the amount you can carry.
   Even with a strength of 18/** or 25 you can only realistically carry
   50000 gold (which will give you just 50000 more points)
3) Dungeon diving: You get 50 additional points (or something like that) for
   each level you make it to, but with only 50 levels, you can only get a
   few thousand points this way.
4) If you ascend to Demigod(dess)hood, your score (from killing monsters
   at least) will be doubled. This of course can only be done once.
5) Gems: Again you can only get at most 4500 points for a gem and can only
   carry about 100 or so at any one time, and besides, valuable gems are very
   rare. (Note that your score from gems won't be doubled if you ascend.)

Now I have seen from some of the high score lists posted that some
have apparently made anywhere from 10-100 million points. So there
must be some way around the limitations of one of the methods of
gaining points above. Number 1 is limited by the time we have to play
and Numbers 2, 3 & 4 are limited by the number of levels/gold pieces
that exist in the game. So to get zillions of points we would
apparently have to (ab)use Number 5 in some way, and find some way of
ascending with lots and lots of gems.

The key spoiler in getting zillions of points lies in the bag of
holding ruse. From this you can give yourself almost unlimited
carrying capacity, which will allow you to carry the thousands of
valuable gems to the endgame.


** First, how to increase your carrying capacity from bags of holding:

As the spoiler file indicates, "Blessing or cursing a non-empty bag of
holding doesn't properly adjust the weight of the bag". Remember that
bags of holding allow you to carry things at (don't know the exact
statistics) half their normal weight, cursed bags of holding are a bit
worse, while blessed bags of holding allow things to be carried at
just 1/4 (or so) of their normal weight. The weight of the bag is
increased by the appropriate amount based on the cursed/blessed state
of the bag when you put an object in, and is decreased by the
appropriate amount when an object is removed. So what you do to take
advantage of this "feature" is to insert a bunch of stuff in the bag
when it is blessed (so that the bag isn't very heavy) and then remove
it while the bag is cursed (which makes the bag *much* lighter). Doing
this can make the bag have a negative weight, which will drastically
increase your carrying capacity. What you do is:

Take a blessed (empty) bag of holding (probably gotten from a
polypile) and insert as many rocks (or gems which will have the same
weight) as you can carry into it. Then curse it and remove the
rocks/gems. Note that a cursed bag of holding will occasionally notify
you that "something has disappeared" and that object will be gone, so
you only want to use rocks or something else you can risk losing. Once
you've removed the rocks, the weight of the bag will be negative, and
you can carry much more stuff. You can then re-bless the bag and
repeat the process (with even more rocks because you can carry a lot
more now) until you are able to carry the many needed gems to the
endgame. Note that it's wise to use a charge of a wand of
cancellation to help un-bless/un-curse the bags (which won't affect
the contents of the bags any) to help save your potions.

A few details: Note that since your inventory items are labeled from
[a-z][A-Z] you can at most carry 52 different objects (inventory
slots) at any one time. Don't worry about going over the limit (which
you can easily do when you have the bags of holding with you) for the
game will say that your "pack is full". Also, if your total weight
gets too negative (like if you can pick up 3000 or so gems at once)
then the game will tend to act funny in that you won't be able to hit
even the simplest monsters any more (perhaps if you get too light and
it affects your hit probability somehow). If ever happens, don't
worry- just pick up some more junk to make yourself heavier or else
drop one of the rigged bags of holding if you made more than one.

It's a lot of fun to be able to pick up massive amounts of stuff, like
three dragon corpses and dozens of food rations at once! It's easy to
bring all those corpses to the altar to give to your God, and easy to
build up massive polypiles (put the stuff you're gathering in a bag
when your pack gets full).


** Second, how to get thousands of valuable gems:

The most valuable gems in the game are dilithium crystals which are
worth 4500 gold pieces, and so always 4500 points each (irrespective
of charisma, etc) if you can finish the came with them (these are
always white). Next comes diamonds (white) for 4000, rubies (red) for
3500, and sapphires (blue) for 3000. In general, to up your score
significantly, you will only want to keep the most valuable of the
gems, such as the top four mentioned above. (Drop them in shops to
determine the gems from the glass, and the most valuable from the
least valuable gems of a particular color.)

The goal now should be to get as many rocks (several thousand) as
possible, and pile them up and polymorph them until you get the gems.
(If you ascend with 1000 dilithium crystals, you will get 4,500,000
additional points.) You will probably want to have several piles with
the rocks separated into groups of a few hundred each so you can
quickly find and identify the various gems. Note that you can get
yourself some luckstones from the rock polypile (and beware)
loadstones, too. You will probably want to have the rocks piled with
your main polypile in the game, so you can polymorph a bunch of other
stuff at the same time, such as many other wands into new wands of
polymorph to keep the pile going. (Note that there is only a 1.82%
chance of polymorphing a particular rock/gem into one of the most four
valuable ones, so you need a pretty big pile of rocks and wands to
keep the pile going.)

Now, how do we get thousands of rocks? The easiest way is to not kill
all the dwarves and rock moles (and umber hulks later on) in the
level, which leave rocks and boulders lying around as they tunnel.
It's best to let them run around rampant until the entire level is
cleared out and you can literally walk around everywhere on the level!
Note that if you've already met the Wizard, when you periodically are
surrounded with monsters, often some of them will be umber hulks, so
don't kill them and let them help clean out the level too. So, now run
around on the level(s) and gather up all the rocks. Use a pick-axe on
the boulders (and any statues that are around) and get 50 or so rocks
per boulder. Note that you can polymorph boulders into statues, but
the statues generally yield less rocks, and you can't get spellbooks
from the polymorphed statues (at least I've never got any). If you've
already rigged up your bag(s) of holding you can carry 100's or 1000's
of rocks at once and quickly build up the pile.

-
In a (pl10) Wizard game I recently finished, I had only 2,300,000
points when I offered the amulet. However, after clearing out one & a
half dungeon levels for rocks (getting 5000 or so rocks per level), I
took 6900 of the most valuable gems with me, and my final score for
the game was 32,100,000 points! I also had (and this shows the power
of intense polypiling) - 23 pages of stuff in my polypile, 26 amulets
of life saving, all 17 named weapons, 35 fully charged wands of
polymorph (not counting 14 additional ones I used all the charges in),
15 magic markers, 4 wands of death, a couple dozen blank scrolls and
potions, 109 food rations, and all the different kinds of good armor
and rings. A diligent player could easily break the 100 million mark.

However, the game wasn't completely a walk in the park, in that one
time I forgot and tried to put a wand of cancellation in one of my
bags of holding and lost in the explosion the wand, the bag, and all
the bag's contents (fortunately they were all replaceable). Also, to
make the game interesting, I made the decision that I was going to
ascend with 4 pet Elementals, one of each type; this was pretty hard,
because I had to find and tame them, as well as get them to go to the
endgame with me (you can only have 2 leashes in use at any one time)
and keep them alive while I was going across to my altar; and while
they were swarming all over me like a bunch of hyper puppies when I
was trying to coax them all one space away from me so I could offer
the amulet, I hit a wrong key and fell in the moat - saved by one of
my amulets, but still you have to be careful even with a tough
character. I could just see Dave H. laughing his head off about those
nethack abusers getting what they deserve, etc. However, getting gems
and rigging up bags of holding was very *fun*, and much more exciting
than reverse genociding rock trolls and killing them over and over.
And as long as we're still having fun, we'll still be playing nethack..

